    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "First of all, it's very important, obviously, that we have a Clean Water Act, a tool for promoting economic development and, of course, drinking water and other efforts in the country. And there's been a lot of confusion about the Clean Water Act for a number of years. And I've been concerned that farmers and ranchers and foresters have had a lot of confusion about what they can do and not do. So I weighed in very heavily with EPA to make sure that they went back because their first round draft was very confusing. And I weighed in very heavily to make sure that the longstanding exemptions for farming, ranching, forestry activities uh... work clearly in place and they now are so uh... i think we thought to be vigilant but i would much rather have those exemptions in place and have uh... farmers have the certainty of uh... knowing you know what uh... is expected of them",
