  {
    "episode_id": 72789,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72789.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, for me, when I look at the fact that I believe we don't have an economy unless we make things and grow things, this is a complicated proposal. When we look at the number of countries involved, the impacts, obviously from an agricultural standpoint, there's a lot of opportunities as well as some concerns, but a lot of opportunities. We are from a manufacturing auto standpoint concerned that particularly in the Asian countries where they use currency manipulation to undercut price, that there's no real enforcement currency manipulation as a trade violation. And so that's a great concern. It's unusual to see any of the auto companies come out against a trade agreement because they're global, but we have seen that happen because of the way this is written. So it's complicated for me. I certainly support trade. We're in a global economy. I want it to be fair for us. And I want to make sure that we're exporting our products, not our jobs.",
