    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72789.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, I agree that using our new technology, what's called a QR code, we already have the codes on the back of most products here as you're going to check out with the price and so on. I think many, many companies are stepping up with very impressive websites providing a lot of different information that consumers are interested in. And there really is a way to connect those things. And so USDA has also been a very thoughtful way working with folks on how that might be done. So I do believe that there's a way to use technology in a way that gives consumers the information that they need and want and does it in a straightforward way that doesn't stigmatize biotechnology and would cut out this, I think, impossible situation of a 50-state patchwork of labeling laws.",
